{"name":"Aqua Green","hex":"#12e193","fetched":"2026-11-01","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aqua","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water (as a compound).","A shade of colour, usually a mix of blue and green, most often similar to the colour cyan, though also sometimes closer to turquoise or aquamarine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greenish-blue colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aqua"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aqua (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is a variation of the color cyan. The normalized color coordinates for the two web colors named aqua and cyan are identical. It was one of the three secondary colors of the RGB color model used on computer and television displays. In the HSV color wheel aqua is precisely halfway between blue and green. However, aqua is not the same as the primary subtractive color named process cyan used in printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg/330px-Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(color)","wikidata":"Q372733"},{"title":"Aqua (Chicago)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is an 82-story mixed-use skyscraper in Lakeshore East, downtown Chicago, Illinois. Designed by a team led by Jeanne Gang of Studio Gang Architects, with James Loewenberg of Loewenberg & Associates as the Architect of Record, it includes five levels of parking below ground. The building's eighty-story, 140,000 sq ft (13,000 m2) base is topped by a 82,550 sq ft (7,669 m2) terrace with gardens, gazebos, pools, hot tubs, a walking/running track and a fire pit. Each floor covers approximately 16,000 sq ft (1,500 m2)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Aqua_%28Chicago%29_logo.png/330px-Aqua_%28Chicago%29_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(Chicago)","wikidata":"Q622895"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg/500px-Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg/1280px-Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg/500px-Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aqua colored sea waters in the Andaman and Nicobar Islands","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg/500px-Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg/1280px-Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg/500px-Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAqua_(Building)_cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/AquaTower2009_02_08_image2.jpg/250px-AquaTower2009_02_08_image2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/AquaTower2009_02_08_image2.jpg/500px-AquaTower2009_02_08_image2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/AquaTower2009_02_08_image2.jpg/250px-AquaTower2009_02_08_image2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.